{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>And when the cloud lingered.</b> The verse explains to you the merit of Israel in being guided by the cloud, for there were in the desert diverse places — some agreeable and some not agreeable — and the proof of this is Marah and Elim. There were agreeable places where they would want to linger, but as soon as the cloud lifted they would journey on; and there were places that were not agreeable and they would want to set out from them, but when the cloud lingered they were obliged to remain and not travel. In sum, they did not go after their own will but after the will of HaShem, may He be exalted, and according to the guidance of the cloud. And furthermore, the verse explains to you the kindness of the Holy One, blessed be He, with them: that all their journeyings and encampments in the desert took place only by day. That is what it says: 'or a day or a night' — and it should have said 'or a night or a day,' for thus is the order of Genesis. But had it said thus, the implication would be that the beginning of their journeying was by night, and this never occurred — that the cloud would settle at night and the day after it, so that their journeying would be by night. And the Holy One, blessed be He, did not wish to burden them by having the start of their journeying and encamping always be by night, but rather by day."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:31:00.969853060Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}